{"trans": "Advocate fair competition, oppose mutual deceit, and promote a thriving and diverse internet; advocate unity and cooperation, oppose harming others for personal gain, and promote mutual benefit and win-win outcomes on the internet."}
{"trans": "In short, perhaps more overseas companies believe that listing in the U.S. is not worth the trouble, and therefore choose to withdraw, but this certainly doesn't mean they are ready to abandon the U.S. market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a market environment filled with nervousness and fear, it would be extremely difficult for gold to remain unscathed; even talking about breaking through the $1000 barrier is likely another pipe dream."}
{"trans": "Police officers explained that these students' actions were examples of righteous bravery; they courageously stepped forward during the critical moment when the elderly man fell into the water, which was highly commendable. It is understood that the elderly man has a mild mental illness. After the hospital's full rescue efforts, he has stabilized and is now safe."}
{"trans": "Of course, the above methods are just a few of the limited yet effective strategies in review. The arrangements for the review sprint phase should be diverse and varied, with numerous approaches available, and should also be tailored to the unique characteristics of each examinee. Wishing all candidates a victorious start and swift success!"}
{"trans": "Flowed into another river of this life and this world,  \nThe place where Zhao Jun dismounted,  \nRiding on the stones of history, still speaking—  \nThe grass is green as in those days,  \nThe flowers still carry the fragrance of the past.  \nA herd of cattle and sheep, unaware of the present day,  \nBow their heads, humble and cautious.  \nIn the meticulous passage of time, drinking water and thinking of its source,  \nPeople sit amidst the fragrance of wine;  \nThe autumn waters of Nanhu, the night is smokeless."}
{"trans": "This belief is not about living in comfort nor seeking longevity. Since humans cannot live twice, how can one realize the meaning and value of life before death? Even if it means being shattered into pieces, one must leave a resounding echo like jade striking the ground with a golden sound, and spark the light of life in the world."}
{"trans": "Other people were still able to remain calm, quickly drew their guns, and scanned the surroundings for enemies, while Li Wenbin alone was in a fluster, diving headfirst into the grass, his backside up in the air, hands covering his head, looking utterly disheveled. His companions covered their faces and snickered, and Li Wenbin's credibility plummeted instantly."}
{"trans": "The animals skeptically asked, \"How do you plan to be king?\" \"First, mediate disputes impartially and fairly. Second, manage state affairs diligently and tirelessly. Third, when facing strong enemies, lead the charge at the forefront. This is my governance speech.\""}
{"trans": "He is worldly-wise and has endured the vicissitudes of life, yet able to turn like a compass needle; his guiding star is ever-changing and not fixed. Thanks to his honeyed words that please others, he has despicably never met with misfortune; plus, he speaks with a silver tongue, never ceasing—except when not paid enough."}
{"trans": "When I first followed my colleague to the stock exchange, it was fate that bound me inseparably to stocks. Seventeen years have allowed me to fully taste the bitterness and sweetness of the stock market. After enduring many ups and downs, I have become a seasoned veteran, with vivid memories of the past! I. The sea of suffering is boundless; turn back and find salvation."}
{"trans": "The defeated general fled for a long time before finally stopping. He looked up to the sky and sighed, \"I rose to power at the age of twenty-five, never tasted defeat in battle, and never failed to capture a city. Now, in my twilight years, I suffer such a crushing defeat! It truly enrages me!\" The news of the victory at the Defense of Ningyuan reached the imperial court, filling the entire court with joyous celebration. Everyone raised their cups in triumph."}
{"trans": "Newlyweds have been receiving a steady stream of friends and relatives offering blessings. Since the living room decor should not be overly unconventional, comfort and warmth should be the focus. It should not only ensure the couple's own comfort but also make guests feel at home. Soft fabric sofas and throw pillows are essential elements."}
{"trans": "I said, \"Let's not generalize; let's just stick to the matter at hand.\" My son replied, \"Over the years, I've observed you critically and feel that you treat computers as too sacred. You don't dare to touch this, and can't even move that. The biggest mental barrier for mothers like you when learning is that you worship computers as deities.\""}
{"trans": "Always living in fear, afraid of saying the wrong thing, doing the wrong thing, or offending others. During the Seven Precepts of Sorrow, unfortunate events from one's life often resurface, involuntarily bringing forth waves of sadness. The Eighth Precept of Doubt refers to those with a suspicious nature, who always believe others are scheming against them, needing to be cautious with every word and action, thus feeling restless and suffering frequent insomnia."}
{"trans": "At the next disgraceful corner stands a pitiful guillotine, sneaking about anxiously and shamefully, seemingly always on edge, as if dreading being caught red-handed while committing its evil deeds—because each time it finishes its dirty work, it immediately sneaks away. How comforting it must be to witness all this!"}
{"trans": "At this moment, the true charm of fighting lies in the sleepless vigil awaiting dawn after a challenge, the taut tension before the clash, the verbal sparring during mediation, the conviviality of clinking cups after the battle, the unwavering loyalty when meeting again, and the solidarity of fighting side by side in future skirmishes. This cycle repeats endlessly, and the ranks of pacifists grow ever stronger."}
{"trans": "The Baron's audacious humiliation is almost unbearable; just you wait, you disgraceful rogue; for the sake of honor, I will take up the responsibility of revenge. The audacious insults from all can only be avenged by him; even if it costs my life, I will not endure in silence."}
{"trans": "It seems there won't be an argument, no storm; now it is calm and peaceful. But the mother once again asks an ill-timed question: \"Do you want to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" The daughter's response is also strange and equally ill-timed: \"Later, dear mother, later.\""}
{"trans": "In dealing with the world, he is still at a beginning stage; however, when it comes to scholarly knowledge, he is fully confident. Even if the director is eloquent, he might not be as sharp-tongued as the professors at a master's thesis defense. Ask a woodcutter how to eat Western food, and he may be at a loss; but ask him how to cut firewood—isn't that a piece of cake for him?!"}
{"trans": "\"You'll soon reap the consequences of your idleness,\" said the plow ox, and continued lowering its head under the yoke, pulling its cart loaded with fertilizer away. You should live a righteous and honest life, always being mindful throughout your life to avoid laziness and idleness. If you still do not feel ashamed, then you will surely reap the consequences."}
{"trans": "Capture it in art, and do so with such vivid realism and lifelike precision. His art repeatedly deceived the eyes, causing people at first glance to mistake it for reality, never suspecting it was a painting. For centuries, painting had been deemed lowbrow and vulgar, unfit for refined circles, but under his hand, it was revived and flourished once more."}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors were often mythologized, becoming sacred and untouchable, mysterious and unfathomable, prompting people to worship them with utmost reverence as if they were deities, thus giving rise to the title \"Son of Heaven.\" In reality, emperors were also human beings, with both virtues and flaws. Among them were wise rulers of great talent and vision who stabilized the nation, as well as corrupt and incompetent tyrants."}
{"trans": "Once, he laughed aloud, head raised to the sky as he departed, proudly chanting, \"We are not born to be commoners!\" The mutual deceit of officialdom, the hypocrisy of society, and the merciless reality cooled his fervent heart. Could the golden signboard of \"imperial scribe\" truly cage your untamed spirit? Finally, after enduring the setbacks and sorrows of a bureaucratic career, you found peace."}
{"trans": "\"A vagabond with suspicious behavior has been harassing our territory for quite some time, stirring up trouble and sowing discord. You are ordered to apprehend this troublemaker and bring him to justice by tomorrow and impose the death penalty upon him.\" \"We will certainly comply, sir,\" replied the police officers before leaving. The villain, being one-eyed, failed to notice that the officers exchanged knowing glances while responding."}
{"trans": "Americans have never deified their national leaders, nor blindly followed them. Yet Obama yielded to his supporters' expectations. He too came to believe he was the savior they had long awaited. The people's silence delivered a jolt. But the intoxicating feeling of such a meteoric rise nearly caused him to lose his bearings."}
{"trans": "The usually approachable Taurus man, with his thoroughly pragmatic nature, cannot stand betrayal from within. Don't even think about testing his sincerity. This steadfast bull is content to graze peacefully and smile at you, much like Jesus gazing at his flock. If you don't want the scene to shift suddenly to a Spanish bullring, with blood flowing like a river and chaos everywhere, then never provoke his jealousy."}
{"trans": "If Geminis don't play a few small tricks or show a bit of cunning, where would the fun in life be? Don't be fooled by their usual laid-back demeanor; once the situation becomes complicated, they will strike you with an unexpected move. While everyone else is fighting fiercely, heads bloodied, they can sit back and reap the fisherman's reward. But once they have successfully captured everyone's attention, they act like a carefree prince, departing stylishly and playing the trick of \"wanting to capture but pretending to let go.\""}
{"trans": "In reality, being part of the Eurozone and tied to the euro, it is simply a fantasy for Germany to think it can remain unaffected. When the Eurozone was initially established, there was a grand vision of shared prosperity; today, however, the Greek debt crisis has triggered a broader European debt crisis, making widespread losses only natural. A fire at the city gate inevitably scorches the fish in the pond, and matters are now even worse with flames engulfing the entire region, turning some areas nearly into scorched earth."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, directly investing in commodities may be the most direct and effective way to hedge against inflation. However, when talking about commodity investments, people often first think of shocking stories—such as those who lost their entire fortunes speculating in commodity futures, or airlines that suffered massive losses hedging with crude oil futures. These examples are numerous, making commodity investments seem so risky that they intimidate ordinary investors."}
{"trans": "The vast sky, having endured the ravages of lightning and thunder, enjoys calm and sunshine. The boundless ocean, having tolerated the fierce storms, gains gentle ripples. The serene forest, having accepted the cruelty of the survival of the fittest, blossoms with birdsong and floral fragrance. The sky, ocean, and forest exemplify that through understanding tolerance, knowing when to retreat, and humbly embracing adversity, beauty and greatness emerge. Bowing low reveals a world of boundless horizons."}
{"trans": "Surveying the ever-changing landscape of recent college entrance exams, we must firmly grasp the new trends and directions in exam question setting, plan ahead, and progress from seeing through a fog to seeing clearly, so that you will command a hundred thousand elite troops within, and on the battlefield, with a smile, the enemy is vanquished and scattered to the winds. Expert guidance turns iron into gold; a journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step; a towering nine-story pagoda starts from its foundation. Let this assist you in taking that crucial first step toward success in preparing for the college entrance exam!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate yourself is like possessing the golden key to happiness. Appreciating yourself is not self-admiration, nor is it selfishness, nor is it self-indulgence, and certainly not complacency. Give yourself some confidence, give yourself some joy, give yourself a smile—why worry about lacking happiness in life? Frequently celebrate your own achievements and learn to cultivate a cheerful spirit."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people are increasingly realizing that the internet and traditional industries are not adversaries in a zero-sum game, but rather a perfectly matched pair capable of complementing each other. The retail industry is exhibiting trends of channel integration, with the mutual penetration and combination of online and offline aspects gradually increasing. Currently, Taobao has opened physical stores, while traditional enterprises rushing to enter the internet are too numerous to list exhaustively. Examples include GOME, Suning Appliance, Walmart, and Carrefour supermarkets, among others."}
{"trans": "In summary, the commodity markets are faced with an endless stream of uncertain factors, financial hegemony continues to manipulate the markets, and the rules of the game change overnight. Against the backdrop of a global debt crisis and a mixed outlook for global economic recovery, the US dollar remains the most significant factor influencing the trajectory of commodities. Economic policies in Europe and the US closely follow suit, while domestic regulatory measures further fuel the momentum. The intertwined interaction of these three factors—liquidity and confidence—will inevitably cause sharp fluctuations in commodity markets."}
{"trans": "Chinese red is a profound spiritual culture unique to the Chinese people. It represents a powerful force characterized by relentless self-improvement, sincerity, diligence, kindness, and perseverance—a noble and enduring quality passed down for thousands of years. Liantianhong, a leading furniture enterprise, passionately spreads the essence of Chinese red, embracing integrity as its core business principle. The company pioneered transparent workshop production, setting an example for the industry and bringing a fresh new look to the furniture sector."}
{"trans": "Physical Characteristics: In \"Journey to the West,\" Master Tang has a tall stature, graceful manners, a kind-hearted nature, and profound knowledge of Buddhism. Despite encountering eighty-one trials during his journey to India to obtain the Buddhist sutras, he remained steadfast. With the assistance of his disciples—Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Wujing—he endured countless hardships and ultimately retrieved the true sutras. Sun Wukong, also known as the monk name Wukong, is Master Tang's eldest disciple. He has fiery golden eyes, the ability to transform seventy-two times, and can ride on clouds and fog. He hates evil as one would hate enemies, fears no difficulties, is resolute and persevering, and is courageous and fearless."}
{"trans": "III. Approach to Studying: I have my own set of methods—\"cultivating problem intuition\" and \"avoiding staying up late.\" In fact, once studying becomes second nature through practice, although you may not be able to solve problems instantly, you can still feel confident. I don't advocate the sea of problems approach because there's no need to repeatedly solve identical or similar problems. We only need to deeply compare and reflect on similar problems, summarizing the methods for solving such types. The so-called \"problem intuition\" is similar to the \"language sense\" often mentioned in English learning."}
{"trans": "The Great Wall of China, the longest man-made structure in the world, is magnificent and grand. Spanning across the rugged mountains of northern China, it has a total length of over 6,700 kilometers. Its construction began during the Spring and Autumn and Warring States periods. This ancient military defensive structure is a rare achievement in human architectural history, renowned for its long history, massive scale, and majestic presence. It has been inscribed by UNESCO on the World Heritage List and is hailed as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World.\""}
{"trans": "Because they have capital, they maintain a low profile; because they stand out from the crowd and refuse to follow common trends, they maintain a low profile. At their core, luxury products are outstanding and even unique, never compromising on quality or the embodiment of fashion, and possess impeccable superiority in both artistic culture and stylistic culture. Luxuries are certainly not necessities in life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and substantial brand heritage can indeed make them indispensable in daily life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as if they were filled with lead, she still strode quickly across the street toward the parking garage. Now, drowsy and driving alone, she traveled along the fluorescent-lit cement lanes, feeling her consciousness fade. Seventeen hours earlier, when she had parked here, two minivans were parked on either side, so close together that she had to awkwardly squeeze out of her car. Now her old Taurus stood alone like an orphan in the eighth-level parking area."}
{"trans": "Ten years ago, perhaps no one could have imagined that the Internet could become mobile with notebook computers, just as twenty years ago people could not envision telephones fitting into pockets and constantly accompanying modern life and work. Today, a variety of smart terminals are exuding unprecedented magic, subtly transforming human lifestyles. In the next decade, within fields such as terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics, many more disruptive innovations are likely to emerge!"}
{"trans": "We advocate team spirit, and we also uphold heroic acts of selflessly rescuing comrades; however, we must ensure that we do not become a burden or encumbrance to our comrades, doing our utmost to prevent them from taking unnecessary risks to rescue us. Therefore, rigorous training and the ability to make prompt decisions on the scene are absolutely essential! Before you have experienced the gunfire and dangers of actual combat, don't show off your armchair theories in front of us. Some things are simply beyond the understanding of fresh-out-of-school cadets like you!"}
{"trans": "I regret that I have not deeply grasped the five-character poem of the poplar tree or my grandfather's seven-character poem. Although I have gradually improved in the art of \"feigning ignorance,\" I still haven't achieved complete clarity. Last night, my neck was bitten by a mute mosquito, so I shouted loudly, \"How can you bite someone without making a sound? How can you suck blood without honesty and openness? How can't you learn to be a righteous mosquito, charging bravely toward my neck with a roar?\" Thus, I live a weary and absurd life, constantly hearing the mosquitoes' mocking hum."}
{"trans": "As barbecue stalls spring up like mushrooms after rain in every corner of the city, the nights have become increasingly vibrant. However, it's truly difficult to find both delicious food and an elegant environment simultaneously. When the sun sets and the red sky meets the lush green grass of the golf course, tables are neatly and thoughtfully arranged according to the contours of the land. Skilled chefs expertly grill the food, waiters and waitresses weave through the crowd, and customers chat happily, all clearly enjoying themselves. Soothing music plays softly in the background, creating a truly romantic and charming atmosphere."}
{"trans": "After hearing my words, the old gentleman sighed deeply, saying, \"Ah, I've cheated death countless times—it's truly impossible to put into words!\" Thus, this proud and headstrong old man finally, for the first time, opened up to me, a writer he had never met before, revealing his tumultuous life and inner world. Through his narrative—sometimes passionate, sometimes somber, sometimes tearful, sometimes bursting with laughter—I experienced the grand, tumultuous, yet tragic life of this septuagenarian weathered by hardships, and his inescapable submission to fate's whims…"}
{"trans": "Thus, it appears that Western politics is far from as clean and incorrupt as people imagine. Beneath the surface of integrity flows a current of murky corruption, albeit with a distinctly Western flavor. Publicly, politicians espouse lofty ideals, while in private they reap lawful benefits. Calculating politicians and astute capitalists work together seamlessly and unspokenly, engaging in mutual favors and money-for-power deals with such finesse that these practices become open and legal. So refined are these tactics that even Western democracy and the rule of law are powerless to address them."}
{"trans": "After hiking through water for hours, a vast cavern suddenly revealed itself. \"Wow, this isn't just a cave; it's exactly like an underground forest!\" shouted the team members. The cavern was as large as a basketball court, its ground littered with jagged rocks, trickling streams, and deep ravines. Stone pillars as thick as a bowl's rim rose ten meters high, and enormous stone curtains, uneven stalactites, and intricately entwined stone columns filled the space—bizarre and varied in shape, just like a primitive forest. With countless crystalline formations sparkling under the lights, walking through the cavern felt as if entering a fairy tale world."}
{"trans": "The heart's scale can also shrink to an extremely small size, capable of holding only a home, a single person, a sesame seed, or a drop of virus. A thread of rain can flood it; a wisp of wind can shatter it. A single rumor can plunge it into unbearable pain; a single conspiracy can cast it into irreversible ruin. The heart can be harder than any metal known in the world. The heart can be soft, melancholic as a lament, delicate as silk or satin. The heart can be resilient, enduring hundreds of setbacks and grievances, yet still remain as smooth as new. The heart can also be fragile; a single misstep, and it instantly shatters into pieces."}
{"trans": "Strolling through this space, one finds lush trees casting dappled shade, vibrant blossoms vying in splendor, and serene tranquility—a breathtaking beauty beyond measure. Gentle breezes carry refreshing fragrances, instantly invigorating the spirit. Stone-paved paths wind into secluded depths, while artfully arranged flowers and trees stand in graceful disarray, accompanied by the crisp, melodious murmur of flowing streams. Multiple vistas interweave in three-dimensional harmony, forming a vivid, living scroll of vibrant life. Each step reveals a new scene: every flower, leaf, blade of grass, tree, stone, and spring exudes a unique charm, transporting one from worldly clamor and allowing the soul to experience the unity of heaven and earth in a beauty that purifies the spirit. Wandering amidst such splendor, one savors fully the bliss of earthly delights."}
{"trans": "The original whaling ship, in a rage, said, \"This is the whale we caught.\" The current whaling ship, smugly, said, \"Then why is it here with us?\" The angry side said, \"It escaped again.\" The smug side said, \"Who told you not to tie it down securely?\" The angry side said:"}
{"trans": "Your hypocritical exterior cannot conceal your arrogance and greed! Pretentious doctors, babbling witches, and glib-tongued swindlers are mocking our helplessness—beware the slap! You, ungrateful husbands, who think yourselves shrewd and capable, disregarding love and kindness;"}
{"trans": "A farce that lasted two months has quieted down. Why Foxconn is so furious about these two reports remains unclear. Well-resourced companies are not short of think tanks; crisis management tactics can extend beyond tearful apologies to include bold displays of anger: perhaps to make an example of one to warn many, or perhaps to feint east and strike west."}
{"trans": "When it comes to rewarding merit, the delicacies should rightfully belong to it. \"I find you pitiable and laughable,\" the wild duck replied, \"so arrogant and conceited. Your view is biased. We wild ducks fly all over the world, free and unfettered, making the entire world our home. Yet you live under someone else's roof; we earn our own living, while you beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "The beginning of an article is the hardest part; it must be sudden and vigorous, direct and forthright, striking the core issue immediately in order to captivate the reader. There's no need to beat around the bush or use clichéd expressions. He also told me that when a logical argument reaches an impasse, introducing a metaphor can effortlessly untangle all complicated debates. What efficiency! What skill! Numerous insights like this exist."}
{"trans": "She solemnly began the divination ritual. After some bustling activity, she pretended to scrutinize the sand tray and calculated the results once more. Then she lifted her head, glared at Kudi, and declared, \"You accursed, despicable wretch! How dare you speak such reckless lies before me! The divination clearly reveals that you are named Kudi, a bandit who murders and pillages, commits every conceivable atrocity, and is utterly beyond redemption.\""}
{"trans": "The castle indeed proved to be a paradise beyond the mundane world. As he beheld the magnificent architecture, his heart and soul were drawn to it, filled with both awe and envy. They strolled through the garden, picking fresh fruits to eat, and were enchanted by the melodious birdsong and fragrant flowers, so captivated that they could hardly tear themselves away. After leisurely exploring the entire castle, night had fallen, so they returned to the hall by the pond, intending to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The air conditioning is indeed effective. The cool, fresh air, the orderly layout, the well-dressed guests, and the courteous waiters all make this place feel like a hidden paradise, exceptionally comfortable. The ones who spoil the ambiance are always the people. Those well-dressed men all have oil-streaked faces from eating, which is quite unpleasant to look at. They all nodded at Nikola, and for some reason, some even gave him a knowing wink."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver, realizing their situation was hopeless and the tide of battle irrevocably lost; they finally gave up resistance and fled toward the city. The armored trains continued shuttling back and forth, clearing out the remaining enemies. They were like two mighty, triumphant dragons of the land, advancing relentlessly, easily crushing all opposition, leveling enemy fortifications into the ground, and sending the slower ones to their deaths. These trains were a stirring victory declaration by the Chinese army, announcing that the day of reckoning had arrived for the stubborn and unyielding invaders."}
{"trans": "After this ordeal, our family never recovered. The family business declined, and we fell into poverty, with the entire family struggling against hunger and cold. The old locust tree also lost its former luster. The remaining half of the tree stump stood solitary in the half-barren courtyard, left alone to endure the wind and rain, the cold dew and frost. Listless for many years, it neither sprouted nor grew branches, ignored by everyone, simply standing there upright, \"sighing to the heavens.\""}
{"trans": "All reactionary forces will not collapse unless you strike them. Dust will not vanish on its own if the broom does not reach it. You are all ruined, except for me, Zhang Pu Jing, the loyal Bolshevik, upright and incorruptible, honest and clean-sleeved, half-hearted, sprawled on my back, prostrate with admiration, everything going smoothly, the July 7th Incident, the Eight Immortals crossing the sea, throughout the land, perfect in every way. Ha ha, revolution is not a dinner party, not writing an article, not painting or embroidery, not frying dough sticks. The proletariat has imposed dictatorship upon you, you ox ghosts and snake spirits."}
{"trans": "Excessive adulation of Gaokao top scorers may lead them to feel superior. Some may develop complacency, arrogance, and self-importance, unconsciously lowering their self-expectations in future work and life, becoming stagnant, and struggling to collaborate with others. Alternatively, others may believe they must never be inferior to anyone at any time, excessively striving for perfection, acting overly cautiously, hesitating to make decisions, and rigidly adhering to rules. All these tendencies may cause former top scorers to lack creativity and passion in their work, ultimately preventing them from achieving greatness."}
{"trans": "I will treat each of my patients equally, regardless of whether their clothes are luxurious or tattered, whether their appearance is handsome or ugly, whether they have abundant wealth or are in financial straits, whether their status is noble or humble, whether they are spotless or scarred, whether they are suffering from complex ailments or merely a minor affliction, whether they are courteous or impolite, whether they possess deep cultivation or are uneducated, whether they are witty and humorous or dull and reserved, whether they are nobles and officials or common folk…"}
{"trans": "Love is free of charge. That involuntary admiration, that irrepressible longing, that profound sentiment of weathering storms together, that sincere devotion of supporting each other in hardship—all of these are life's deepest comfort and most solid foundation. And all of these are free, things money cannot buy.\n\nGoals are free of charge too. Whether you are a prince clad in brocade and feasting on delicacies, or a ragged street child struggling to cover your body, as long as you are willing, you can set a goal for your life. This goal can be grand or modest, brilliant or simple—whatever you choose, you can have it, as long as you are willing."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should focus your energy, plan the path to success, and then move forward with unwavering determination; during this time, you must not be distracted, look around, or become fickle-minded. In this process, you should firmly eliminate all doubt and fear, as they will undermine your fighting spirit, disrupt your drive to move forward, and hinder your efforts to wholeheartedly achieve your objectives. Those filled with doubt and fear will ultimately accomplish nothing and end up with nothing. When the emotions of doubt and fear creep into your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all strong-willed thoughts will be severely shaken and completely collapse."}
{"trans": "A cultivated person holds profound respect, reverence, and admiration for humanity's many outstanding qualities, such as loyalty, bravery, trustworthiness, diligence, mutual assistance, self-sacrifice, fearlessness in times of crisis, endurance, and unyielding integrity. Not everyone may personally embody these virtues, but they know how to honor and praise them. A person may possess cowardice and laziness, but they must not disguise these vices as lofty virtues, nor can they, simply because they themselves cannot achieve nobility, denounce those who do as hypocritical. You may kneel in the mud, but you must not smear the entire world's chest with filth and then solemnly declare that everywhere is dirty."}
{"trans": "In this world, there are beginnings that are quiet and uneventful, beginnings that are grand and spectacular, beginnings that are cautious and meticulous, beginnings that are bold and decisive, beginnings that are hesitant and secretive, beginnings that are half-hearted and reluctant, beginnings that harbor ulterior motives, and beginnings that are open and aboveboard. In every journey of life and in every aspect of living, different people choose their own unique ways to begin. These approaches reflect a person's mindset, vision, courage, composure, and breadth of character in managing their life."}
{"trans": "Typically, the final stage of review plays a pivotal role in the entire preparation process, much like the final flourish that brings everything to life. Therefore, we must place great importance on the final review stage, while also avoiding mistakes that could result in a loss of all progress and narrowly missing success. Below, we will address several common pitfalls that are easy to encounter."}
{"trans": "Currently, the stock market lacks a clear leader, with major sectors adjusting in rotation. Ineffective market defense measures and significant operational challenges for mainstream capital have left the market very weak. Like a bird startled by a bowstring, it panics at the slightest negative news, triggering intensified selling driven by fear. Meanwhile, external funds remain on the sidelines, and with the holiday season approaching, bullish sentiment is weak, further fragmenting market confidence."}
{"trans": "The Japanese, who were making a desperate last stand, were already barely clinging to survival, their barely maintained front line like a warship riddled with holes and taking on water from all sides; after this fatal blow, it immediately shattered like weathered rocks. In fact, stopping the armored train's advance was not difficult; it was simply a matter of demolishing the tracks in advance."}
{"trans": "Passing Off Inferior as Genuine: How to Distinguish Authenticity? Decorative hand walnuts have gained increasing recognition and popularity, with market prices soaring accordingly, while counterfeits made using high-tech methods are also widespread. Initially, Old Hu also fell for fakes, but now, with extensive experience, he even sleeps clutching walnuts every night and is practically immune to deception. He shared several methods for identifying authenticity with readers of the Evening News."}
{"trans": "My life, like that of most people, has seen both broad highways and narrow wooden bridges, traversing ups and downs, twists and turns. I must admit that I have been somewhat fortunate; my achievements and reputation are perhaps somewhat undeserved. On the other hand, my share of misfortune has also been something few others could claim. During that horrifying and shocking so-called \"Great Revolution,\" I nearly lost my life for daring to speak out in defense of justice. The physical suffering I endured is also unforgettable."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang can indeed be regarded as one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. He compared himself to Guan Zhong in Longzhong—what confidence that showed! And how accurate was his prediction of the tripartite division of the empire! Upon his debut, he fearlessly faced Xiahou Dun's army of 100,000 troops. He set fire to the Bowang Slope, convincing Guan Yu and Zhang Fei to wholeheartedly accept his leadership. He burned Xinye, leaving Cao Ren terrified. With clever strategies from brocade pouches and outwitting Zhou Yu thrice, he displayed not only intelligence but also wit. His loyalty was unwavering—he never sought the throne despite Liu Bei granting him special permission. Forced to employ the empty city strategy due to a mistaken decision, his calmness under pressure was truly admirable. However, what moved me most was not any of these, but rather \"the autumn wind at Wuzhang Plains.\""}
{"trans": "As night falls on the mountain village, we hear a cacophony of sharp, intermittent dog barks. Past midnight, the barking becomes faint and indistinct; one after another, lights flicker on in the windows, like the white heart of a cabbage, presenting clean and pure faces. The moonlight was also washing its face by the water pipes in the courtyard..."}
{"trans": "Close-range shots go wide; headers at the goalmouth mysteriously miss; even one-on-one chances are squandered... With insufficient playing time in domestic leagues, the China U-20 national team's frontline ability to seize opportunities evokes sighs, and this is currently the team's biggest weakness."}
{"trans": "But from a sociological perspective, Israelis and Palestinians today are bitter enemies. The reasons lie partly in the mass exodus of Jews from Palestine in 556 BCE and their subsequent dispersal around the world, which separated the two estranged brothers for over a thousand years, breeding unfamiliarity, indifference, suspicion, and hostility. They also stem from the Jews' return to Palestine two thousand years later to establish the state of Israel. As a result, their mutual conflicts escalated into slaughter, and all traces of brotherhood vanished completely."}
{"trans": "National policies descend like thunder from the heavens, the industry's situation takes a sharp downturn, ceramic production regions are the first to bear the brunt, like a trapped beast caught in a dilemma, the production areas are struggling while ceramic enterprises search for a way forward. A cold wave descends, bringing shockwaves and suffering to the production regions, yet also forcing them to see their future path with greater clarity. In-depth reading: As the industry's situation takes a sharp downturn, ceramic production regions struggle like trapped beasts."}
{"trans": "Stepping into the Suzhou garden, wandering through its courtyards, one might encounter small bridges over flowing streams, white walls with dark roof tiles, winding paths leading to secluded spots, twisting trails that turn with the peaks, or shifting views that change endlessly as one walks. The most profound impression is that the meticulous craftsmanship of the garden closely resembles the imperial gardens of the Forbidden City, achieving similar artistic effects through different techniques. Pavilions and waterside pavilions are arranged in a layered progression and artful disarray, creating a sense of depth. Walking along a mere 20-meter path gives the visual impression of strolling through 3 to 5 li of open space, instantly evoking the feeling of moving through a painting."}
{"trans": "The battlefield situation is ever-changing, and since ancient times there has been no fixed rule for securing victory. Deploying troops, appointing commanders, choosing between offensive or defensive actions, positional warfare or mobile warfare, active retreat or holding positions—decisions such as which areas to abandon and which to defend should all be made by the frontline commanders themselves, with minimal interference from the supreme commander. Indeed, any strategic or tactical approach can be integrated and applied flexibly; no single method can be deemed inherently superior. This is precisely what the saying \"All roads lead to Rome\" means—only achieving victory is the ultimate measure of success."}
{"trans": "Novels are the backlight of the soul; you infuse a part of your soul into your work, endowing it with your own flesh and blood, thus achieving artistic height. This involves two issues: first, writers must examine their true spiritual state and prioritize shaping themselves; second, sincerity holds immense power. Here, sincerity's significance not only corrects deviations but also rejects artificiality, fawning, pandering, and opportunistic creative tendencies. Don't beat around the bush, don't overcomplicate simple matters, and don't peddle sincerity like a quack remedy. I believe sincerity should be a way of life, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The weather-beaten locust tree by the window,  \nThe moon returns, motionless in its original place,  \nHanging like a bell upon the still locust branch,  \nYet so far from the sound of the bell.  \nI know, fragments should not hope to strike the ground with golden sound.  \nYet it is these very fragments of moonlight  \nThat make the silent midnight more like midnight—  \nA sunken ship."}
{"trans": "Ruthless and merciless, cold-blooded and heartless, treacherous and sinister—I am instead kind-hearted and lenient, charitable and benevolent, delivering all beings. In the dismal Manor of Dis, my soul was drawing talismans and writing words with intense concentration when suddenly the anguished voice of Dulcinea of Toboso was heard, and only then did I learn that she had unfortunately fallen victim to sorcery."}
{"trans": "Internet analyst Xu Dandan believes that Alibaba is suspected of \"dismantling the bridge after crossing the river.\" \"Capital has its nature, and it is only natural for them to act in the best interests of their shareholders. Accepting an investment means accepting the terms of that capital. One cannot worship it as a deity when it is needed and denounce it as a demon when it becomes an obstacle.\""}
{"trans": "Eyes that can discern the finest details are also helpless! Dazzled and overwhelmed, none dare to look directly at the throne. We come from the East, yet events unfold in the West; the procession is both vast and lengthy—from head to tail its end cannot be seen. Falling forward and surging backward, rushing eagerly to the front, brimming with courage, spears in hand, one fighting ten, ten resisting a hundred, millions of lives disappearing without a trace."}
{"trans": "When he had just seized Zu Bailing and was carried away with joy, he had to go on a long trip for some business. Upon returning home, he learned from his family that Zu Bailing, along with a bag of gold and silver, had vanished into thin air. Upon hearing this news, he flew into a rage, stomping his feet and glaring angrily. He slapped and cursed himself and even tore his own clothes. When he thought about how all his efforts had been in vain, he became even angrier."}
{"trans": "2008 was an extraordinary year. In the battlefield of public relations and marketing for domestic enterprises, there was also intense turmoil and fierce competition. For PR professionals in companies, the \"PR crisis\" seemed to strike overnight, like a flood or ferocious beast, leaving everyone trembling with fear. Time flies forward rapidly; before we know it, we're about to step into 2009. Looking back on this year, many business owners may still feel lingering fear, walking as if on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Leo friends rarely refuse any work requests, as long as these tasks allow them to showcase their talents—they will bite the bullet and help. However, doing so often leads to forgetfulness and an overwhelming workload. Therefore, a handy planner and weekly schedule are the most suitable office essentials to help them stay organized. Especially those with a lively, childlike style will perfectly suit Leo's innocent and youthful nature, enabling them to handle even the busiest times effortlessly."}
{"trans": "An excellent essay should incorporate six or seven types of refined sentences: first, vivid and beautiful metaphorical sentences; second, grand and imposing parallel sentences; third, emotionally rich personification sentences; fourth, culturally rich allusive sentences; fifth, insightful philosophical sentences; sixth, thought-provoking contrast sentences; and seventh, lyrical poetic sentences. Skillfully employing these refined sentences makes expression concise yet meaningful, deeply symbolic, highlights key points effectively, enhances the overall piece, amplifies impact, and naturally elevates the essay's literary quality."}
{"trans": "Even more absurd is that Western countries' economies still remain at a loss, their printing presses itch to print money, and their treasuries are already empty, yet they again expect China to feed the world... Everyone now turns their gaze to China, the world's second-largest economy. If the post-Cold War global order dominated by the United States has already fallen into a desperate struggle for survival, will this emerging economic superpower step forward to take responsibility? Or will it simply let the West reap the consequences of its own actions? This time, however, China may be willing but unable to help."}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for fifty-four years and expanded the nation's territory to encompass a vast domain stretching from eastern Liaodong and central Korea in the east, to the shores of Lake Balkhash today in the west, reaching deep into present-day Vietnam in the south, and extending northward to the Saiyin Mountains in Outer Mongolia. The population under his rule nearly reached sixty million. Objectively speaking, among the hundreds of Chinese emperors, few could match Liu Che's achievements in territorial expansion. Most others were merely able to maintain their rule without becoming traitors who compromised the nation's sovereignty. Judging solely by this criterion, Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, should indeed be regarded as an emperor of great talent and vision."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the trivialities of everyday life among ordinary people, lacking dramatic twists and turns in plot, yet they offer a refreshing new perspective and unmistakable personal inclinations that make them feel entirely new. He excels at creating uniquely individualized characters, which is precisely the hallmark of a genius writer."}
{"trans": "Some people bluff and exaggerate, using big names to prop themselves up, often claiming to be the first in the industry or pioneers to highlight their selling points, incessantly promoting themselves in the sea of information. Others, however, prefer to keep their wealth hidden, focus on self-improvement, maintain a low profile, and build up strength, working diligently without a sound."}
{"trans": "In fact, why do flame wars always erupt on such a massive scale and persist for months without subsiding? What hidden forces are fueling this phenomenon from behind the scenes? And exactly what subtle influences are shaping netizens' judgments and thought processes? Not only are ordinary internet users puzzled by this, but even some website administrators find it completely baffling."}
{"trans": "In the evening, he spread out his manuscript paper. He was preparing to write an article to earn back those 20 yuan. That night, the title of his article was: On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality? He wrote: \"In this decadent age of material desires, we must uphold the banner of morality and oppose the servitude of materialism.\" That night, his essay surged forward triumphantly, passionate and indignant, deeply distressed, patiently persuasive, boiling with fervor, heart-wrenching, sincere and loyal, incisive and unrestrained, flowing smoothly and soaring freely—a torrential outpouring."}
{"trans": "1. Shenlun requires a visionary perspective. As a standard official writing style, the most fundamental characteristic of Shenlun is that its ideas and themes must be lofty. Shenlun writing should focus on long-term interests, see through phenomena to the essence, adeptly take a high-level, commanding view, and skillfully elevate the theme. In other words, the resulting work must embody an elevated ideological realm, avoid catering to vulgarity, and certainly not be vulgar, base, or filled with complaints."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is a compassion for the suffering. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of those who seek unknown things, like stardust falling on a child's eyelashes, and also like a piece of bread in one's throat."}
{"trans": "Look further up, how elegantly proportioned her shoulders are! Like twin lambs, or like two jade peaks; they are as slender as autumn mountains, as smooth as autumn waters. Above the shoulders lies the face, the very center of admiration and praise."}
{"trans": "Even the lotus suffers a tragedy akin to the extermination of nine generations. Lotuses entwine, their petals' thousand fingers clutching one summer, then releasing another. Now comes the ghostly rain of an autumn night, pattering upon the duckweed-dappled water, like a disheveled, sightless Chopin abusing a thousand-keyed piano."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moon, its meaning deepens; speaking of swordsmanship under the moon, sincerity grows; discussing poetry under the moon, elegance becomes more refined; gazing at a beloved under the moon, affection strengthens.  \nThe method of appreciating the moon: when it shines bright, look upward; when it's hazy, look downward.  \nSpring wind is like wine; summer wind is like tea; autumn wind is like smoke; winter wind is like ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He rides the crimson waves of blood, gliding gracefully into this damp and cold world on a red leaf-like skiff. His final leap is propelled through the gates of life by surging waves of heat, like mud and sand swept away in a flood. The infant's frenzied cries shatter like colliding glass cups."}
{"trans": "If China has gained another melancholic writer, this north-facing study should be held responsible. Sitting within the shadow of this northward window, I feel like a fruit brimming with the essence of the south, preserved in a refrigerator. During daylight hours, I seem submerged at the ocean's depths, where silent darkness plays music in shades of gray."}
{"trans": "The red candle possesses a spirit; she does not begrudge her life, yet she clings to it fiercely. Whenever she is nearly consumed, the charred wick arches like a spine, rising high and convulsively in the flame, resisting. She resembles a warrior suddenly struck by a bullet, frozen mid-air into an indomitable sculpture, then sinking heavily into a crimson pool of blood..."}
{"trans": "When you step outside and look up at the sky, its celestial grid reflects your every action. After the morning dew falls and the rain stops, the sun emerges, adorned with glistening pearls that shine together—one sun giving rise to countless suns. The old spiderweb in the corner need not be swept away; let dust settle upon it. Over time, the threads grow thicker, resembling the entwined roots of an ancient tree, forming a three-dimensional mural. Read tradition, read modernity—each time you read, it is ever fresh and new."}
{"trans": "Spring always knocks on the garden's bamboo gate first, then reignites, one by one, the torches extinguished last year. At this moment, winter, left alone in the empty house, becomes like a mournful wolf fleeing in panic from the flames that suddenly blaze up. The fire leaves its lonely gaze bewildered, and the earth's floral dress causes it to lose its way."}
{"trans": "The methods used to punish evil are more wicked than evil itself; slaughtering the innocent is as effortless as cutting leeks. Beneath the banners of loyalty, filial piety, chastity, and righteousness, blades flash and swords gleam; the cost of grandeur is a battlefield littered with corpses. The fundamental value of life is no more than a few dry stalks of grass crushed beneath horse hooves; the people's right to live is but a few fragile bubbles on the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "—Heavenly sound, infinite mystery, the infinite besieging the finite, or the stern yet gentle command of God. Music is the omnipotent and omniscient God of notes, who is both Creator—arranging and defining the positions of the notes—and Savior—if the notes can attentively listen and follow that relentless and tireless resonance."}
{"trans": "Over the winding lotus pond, dense layers of lotus leaves stretch as far as the eye can see. Rising high above the water, they resemble the skirts of graceful dancers. Among these layers of leaves are scattered white blossoms—some elegantly in full bloom, others shyly still in bud; like luminous pearls, like stars in the azure sky, like a beauty fresh from her bath."}
{"trans": "Therefore, in terms of cities, if everything encountered and seen appears youthful and bright, it must mean that the right stage has not yet been reached, and harmony has not yet been achieved—just like writing. When adjectives are like a lady in full makeup, and parallel structures resemble lovers walking side by side, one has certainly not yet entered the realm of true literary craft. The pinnacle of writing is like an ancient street with sparse parasol trees, old seats beneath the trees, and relaxed conversation among those seated—refined yet carefree."}
{"trans": "The suffering of one family does not affect the happiness of the world. Summer arrives irresistibly, and the silk tree flowers, like pink pom-poms, brush against the lonely and desolate hospital windowsill. The girl's head has become polygonal; the long-healed bone sutures resemble cracked earth, black holes gaping beneath her tenuous skin, as an inner demon swells in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a fruit chilled in a refrigerator, pregnant with the essence of the south. By day, I seem to be submerged in the ocean depths, where silent darkness plays gray music. At night, I seem to hear the sleds of the Eskimos, and the North Star's long beard垂d down, ringing out, to strike clusters of white stalactites."}
{"trans": "They are as quiet as the bright moon, not wishing to disturb anyone, yet they truly do stir up a wide area around them. This can indeed be called \"the moon rising and startling the mountain birds.\" Compared to Tao Yuanming's tranquility, Wang Wei's quietness carries a touch more nobility, a touch more refined design. His brilliance lies in being nobler than commoners yet more common than commoners, in crafting designs that feel more natural than nature itself."}
{"trans": "Even the brown coffee table is painted with emotion, a gentle little rectangle bearing all the lively activity upon it. Another larger one features magnolias, thin and luminous, resembling jade and crystal, evoking the cool sensation of the jade fish Yang Guifei held in her mouth during a toothache. The resilient, vigorous lines of the wintersweet flowers stretch and contract; their control over life is both composed and domineering."}
{"trans": "\"Vast and boundless, returning to the great wilderness!\" When I read this passage, it doesn’t evoke sadness but beauty—a feeling akin to reading the Records of the Grand Historian when Jing Ke, dressed in white, crosses the Yi River to assassinate the Qin King. It is filled with vivid colors. Imagine a young man from a wealthy family who has renounced worldly attachments, standing barefoot and bald in the snow, clad in a red cloak, bidding farewell to his father. What a sight of beauty!"}
{"trans": "We cannot move beyond that dark, humiliating, and indifferent Chengde era, just as approaching the Mogao Caves inevitably forces us to face that ugly and desolate Taoist priest tower. No matter how magnificent and splendid Dunhuang appears in our memories, it can never fill the vast emptiness of the Library Cave, can never erase the ghastly pallor of the Caves of the Thousand Buddhas, can never heal the bleeding wounds of ancient ethnicities at the edge of the horizon."}
{"trans": "Forgetfulness visits us with increasing frequency, becoming an inseparable companion until death. I use this companion as a sieve—what is forgotten naturally no longer needs to be remembered. The subconscious manipulates memories, much like wind steering a kite from an unseen level. New warp and weft of intense experiences weave into an uneven sieve of memory; the remaining clumps resemble cheese, sweet and fragrant yet containing gritty, hard bits that irritate the teeth."}
{"trans": "His chest is majestic and upright, echoing the earth-shattering roars of his ancestors chasing fierce beasts. The pelvis is sharply concave, with prominent bones indicating powerful muscles once attached, like the ropes of Yellow River boatmen pulling the entire torso in gecko-like climbing. The limbs resemble the long, beautiful tusks of an African elephant, gleaming with a smooth, lustrous sheen."}
{"trans": "It took several years before I could finally overcome my lingering resentment and admit that that day had been a steep bend in life. It was not the art teacher's mockery that caused me to abandon my withered rose painting, but rather seeing your brilliant talent shining so brightly that I broke my brush myself with a regretful gesture. What is regret like? It is like a small mole on one's body, whose position and emergence are known only to oneself."}
{"trans": "I was combing my hair on the balcony, and strands of hair fell like leaves, dropping in clumps, draping and swaying against my arms like night rain. Car horns were crying out in panic from near and far; the sky was gradually darkening, spreading all around like a vast misty lake. Across the way, from a window opening on the ground floor of a building, a thin wisp of pale smoke curled upward hesitantly, as if uncertain where the sky lay."}
{"trans": "She was holding a kettle in each hand, which again reminded me of a woman striding with vigor on a thin rope. This was entirely due to her waist; her waist was indeed so soft, as I would plainly say, so soft that it felt as if I were eating Suzhou's cowhide candy. Not only her waist—my diary put it well: she possessed curves rivaling the beauty of clouds and mists, and the spirituality of moonlight upon water, weaving a vast web of bewitching charm!"}
{"trans": "Because of your language, you are silent; when sinking to the deepest depth, you make yourself disappear. Having lost language, thus losing the self and the substance of existence, Yang Lian comes to realize he has become a \"ghost\"; a ghost floating between cities, observing coldly (like an insect, a ghost is also an \"it,\" only able to watch from the sidelines), witnessing the complete eradication of \"meaning\" as a concept. There is a sea, yet the harbor holds no meaning for you."}
{"trans": "Streetlight after streetlight stands far apart; between stretches of brightness lie stretches of darkness. My shadow appears in the brightness at times, and at times vanishes into the darkness. The wind arising from nowhere ripples through the vibrant fallen leaves, as if stirring impressions of life. I feel as though I were this hollow wind itself, only able to sense my own existence when causing the colorful fallen leaves to flutter and swirl."}
{"trans": "But we who stood on the open land—my father, my older brother, relatives, and many villagers who had sweated and toiled, been scorched by the sun, and drenched by storms—stood motionless, listening to the distant thunder, with nobody moving to take shelter from the northwest rain. Our hearts were heavier than the parched sky; everyone remained silent, for our hearts too were skies about to rain, and this rain of the heart seemed even more tragic and resolute than the northwest rain, pouring down ceaselessly, linking heaven and earth."}
{"trans": "Imagine if Tang Bohu and Qianlong became recognized as \"first-rate poets of ancient China\"—then we might as well quietly burn the entire collection of \"Complete Tang Poems.\" Calligraphy is no different; a staggering high price assigned to an average piece of work is like piling gold to tip the scales of Chinese calligraphy history. Facing such a situation, I once sighed deeply: \"With the cultural lineage lost, small hills claim to be peaks; with strong wings gone, broken feathers pretend to be a peng.\""}
{"trans": "When it struck, it was sudden, as if the girl had received a divine decree from the heavens, her body convulsing abruptly without warning. The soft girl would shrivel into something as rigid as a noodle-stirring rod, every muscle gleaming like iron. Her tiny body arched like a hawk's bow, recoiling against the deathly pale sickbed, countless droplets of sweat splattering from this grotesque human rainbow, dripping like melting snow from eaves when spring warms and flowers bloom."}
{"trans": "The unleashed power, solitary yet mighty, both following and breaking norms, blending drunkenness with poetic beauty, closely resembles the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu wielded his brush like a staggering drunkard's steps, swaying unsteadily, gesticulating wildly, graceful and vigorous in posture, seamlessly completing all movements in one breath with boundless energy, then cast aside his cup and laughed, sinking into a blissful slumber. Zhang Xu did not realize that his own drunken steps precisely mirrored the rhythm of Tang culture."}
{"trans": "But just as I was holding my breath and focusing intently, suddenly and in unison, they all fell silent—the cicadas startled me again! Like a rope, the cicada's song tightly bound my heart, then suddenly loosened without warning, leaving my heart scattered and unprepared, like a wave straining to leap into the sky, only to accidentally crash down onto the sand! When had summer crossed the threshold and drawn near without my realizing it!"}
{"trans": "I once shed tears in sorrow for your humiliation and disappointment. My tears flowed like a stream, clear as crystal, yet they could not wash away your thick stains of filth, but only swept away the veils from my own eyes; these tears could not moisten your hearts of iron and stone at all, but only doused the anxious, fervent flames within me. Now, in the face of your suffering, I laugh—a laughter like a thunderous roar, not born after the storm, but sounding before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually came to understand that when facing disaster, one cannot use the grammar of disaster; another grammar exists that directly leads to the poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From this moment onward, my state of life became different. Each time I read chapters from Zhuangzi such as \"Autumn Waters,\" \"Free and Easy Wandering,\" \"On the Equality of Things,\" and \"All Under Heaven,\" it felt as though I were looking at electrocardiograms that were intimately related to myself. For such a sage who feels too close to me, I find it difficult to offer a calm and impartial evaluation, and thus can only avoid it to some extent."}
{"trans": "You press your forehead against the gold-threaded embroidery. When the sun was here, it baked the golden threads scorching hot, yet now they have grown cold. The people of the past struggled through their lives, their actions gradually gathering dust; when their descendants hang out clothes, they shake off the dust again, sending it swirling in the yellow sunlight. If memories had a scent, it would be the fragrance of camphor—sweet and soothing, like clearly remembered joys; sweet and wistful, like forgotten sorrows."}
{"trans": "It is precisely this quality that brings them close to life, allowing us even now, thousands of years later, to feel close to them. Yang Guifei's lively presence, I imagine, is like a ceramic hot-water bottle, smooth as jade, placed by one's feet; as the water inside gradually cools, it evokes a gentle wistfulness. Su Qing, however, is like a small red clay brazier, possessing its own independent fire, emitting visible crimson flames, crackling audibly, yet more difficult to tend—requiring constant additions of coal and firewood, its smoke pungent and irritating."}
{"trans": "Like surging waves, like terrifying tides, pounding the emotions settled deep within your heart, in an instant, you feel that the cicada's sound, like a raging torrent sweeping away sand, has snatched from your grasp the light sorrow you so tightly held. The cicada's urgent cry suddenly halts at its highest, most intense note, much like a magnificent literary piece violently torn apart, scattering resounding words across the ground like clashing metal and stone, then silently fading into a lonely, broken fragment, leaving behind only a lingering sense of melancholy, a touch of sadness. Is this not also the song of life?"}
{"trans": "Here abounds vibrant youth and hearts burning with fiery passion; there are no dispirited little old men, only vigorous old youths. The silver-white moon paces restlessly across the vast, hollow sky, as if shedding tears, resentful of her loneliness. ... And there is the swimming pool, forever like a kind old lady, laughing with wrinkled face; when she sees many lively children plunging into the water like little mermaids with plump-plump splashes, she bursts forth joyfully into large silver waves."}
{"trans": "For millennia, it has been a forgotten wasteland; beyond the wasteland are shadowy and unknown great craftsmen, while on this side stands a panic-stricken modern woman. The kilns on both sides blaze fiercely, like two beacon towers separated by mountains and rivers, yet the signals they transmit are precise and error-free. How many other beacon towers have been related to war, but only these two have not; separated by the bloodshed of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang dynasties, and the battles of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing dynasties, there are only two wisps of the purest smoke, echoing each other from afar."}
{"trans": "Lin Daiyu's brokenness lies in her deeply etched love; Sanmao's brokenness originates from a moment of clarity and transcendence after enduring countless trials; Van Gogh's brokenness is the sun's golden blade inflicting relentless agony upon him in the midst of light; Beethoven's brokenness is the spiritual intensity of the black and white piano keys colliding in a tragic and majestic symphony of life. If the brokenness of ordinary individuals reveals the purest and most beautiful glimmers of humanity, then the brokenness of these extraordinary souls resembles silver fireworks blooming across the night sky above us."}
{"trans": "No matter how many times you wash your face in a day, it still isn't clean; yet eyes, never washed, remain forever bright. There's no space left where a mop or broom could function, so there's no need to spend money on them—after all, people themselves are active beings, naturally dust-repellent. Strangely, the air does not feel thin despite the confined space. To visualize the breath of human life, cigarette smoke becomes tangible air: inhaling one breath and exhaling three, its delicate swirls rising to the ceiling like auspicious clouds. After closely observing the richness of life below, one can truly look up to appreciate the vastness of the universe above."}
{"trans": "Knowing oneself without first understanding others is merely a way of gathering in one corner, never interacting until death; it is but the approach of summer insects that cannot speak of ice, frogs at the bottom of a well, or donkeys confined to a mill. Only by understanding others can one truly possess self-awareness; it is just like Princess Iron Fan's fan, which must be able to expand outward before it can contract back again. The more one knows, the broader one's horizons become; by diffusing oneself throughout the world and penetrating all things, observing their size, shape, weight, and density, can one gradually, bit by bit, discern one's own true nature."}
{"trans": "The song flows like drifting clouds and running water, soothing one's cares and allowing one to drift leisurely within. Then like surging tides, like terrifying waves, it pounds the buried emotions deep within your heart. Suddenly, you feel as if the cicada song, like a fierce current sweeping away sand, has snatched from your clenched hands the faint sorrow you held so tightly. The urgency of the cicada's cry abruptly halts at its highest, most intense note, much like a brocade of prose suddenly torn asunder, scattering resounding words across the ground, clattering like the clash of metal and stone. Then silence falls, leaving behind only a fragmentary remnant, offering naught but lingering melancholy and sorrow."}
{"trans": "How can nihilism exist? Divine matters are unknown to humans; human affairs involve, within the confines of fate—helplessly, one might say—constructing and sustaining meaning, thereby saving the present and the eternal. Therefore, \"eternal recurrence\" is by no means \"a complete affirmation of earthly life,\" but rather it merely states that humans cannot escape earthly life, not even through death. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence toward the eternal—that is, the earth's yearning toward the heavens. That grand symphony has always filled heaven and earth."}
{"trans": "Viewing Master Xiaoyun's Zen paintings offers a completely different experience. It feels as though we are reading the pastoral poems of Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei late at night—only a few strokes, lightly inked, unable to stir turbulent emotions within the heart, yet instead calming those very emotions. It does not fill our hearts with something new, but rather washes away the worldly worries already lodged within us, like a mountain stream after a storm. At first the stream runs muddy, yet once the rain has passed and the sky cleared, the water becomes entirely clear, washing away all the mud and filth from the mountainside."}
{"trans": "This sound ebbs and flows, now slow now swift; rises and falls, now high now low; swells and fades, now loud now soft; breaks and resumes, now disjointed now continuous. Sometimes it resounds like golden tones and jade vibrations, sometimes it rings grand and sonorous as ceremonial bells, sometimes it cascades like pearls, large and small, falling on a jade plate, sometimes it sinks deep like red and white corals descending into the ocean, sometimes it dances like an unadorned zither being played, sometimes it crackles like thunderbolts flashing, sometimes it flourishes like a hundred birds vying in melody, sometimes it surges like hares darting and hawks soaring. My thoughts soar in endless imagination; I cannot restrain myself, my heart blossoms exuberantly, and a breeze stirs beneath my pen. Lifeless characters seem to awaken, and I too feel brimming with youthful vitality. Rarely in my life have I reached such a spiritual realm, and words could never fully convey it to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps the clouds were always meant to wander the heavens, unlike the sun which possesses fiery wheels for feet, and thus cannot descend to accept my sincere affection—it is merely an illusion of mine, albeit one perhaps too beautiful. If the blue sky is an unwritten celestial manuscript, then the clouds must be its wordless annotations, and the trail of my speeding car, translating the clouds' language upon the road surface, becomes the latest published commentary. The sky narrates its tale in layers of changing blue, the clouds depict with clean brushstrokes, then deliver their work to my eyes for printing; we are all recounting the story of Kuafu."}
{"trans": "I couldn't conveniently take it out and eat it on the plane. When I returned to the United States and tried it, it was too oily and overly spicy—nothing like the occasional sausage roll my father would make. In Shanghai, right next door to our home was the newly relocated Käsele Café from wartime Tianjin; each dawn they baked bread, setting off an olfactory alarm, as a magnificent aroma burst forth from the sky with the force of a mighty wind sweeping across ten thousand miles. It was the gentlest alarm clock imaginable, yet it rang at the worst times, pointlessly waking people like the vexing beauty of spring that leaves one helpless. Having such a \"fragrant\" neighbor was indeed a nuisance."}
{"trans": "In life, happiness is like a cube of sugar used to tempt a child into taking medicine, or even more like the electric rabbit in a dog racing track that entices the dogs to run. Moments or days of happiness cause us to live through an entire lifetime, enduring much suffering. We hope it will come, we hope it will stay, we hope it will return—these three hopes encapsulate the entire history of human endeavor. While we are pursuing and waiting, life stealthily slips away unnoticed. Perhaps we are merely tokens consumed by time; living through a lifetime is nothing but serving as a sacrificial offering to those years, leaving us with no chance even to consider happiness."}
{"trans": "There is a kind of dark green silk with large black shadows gliding across its surface, teeming with wind and thunder. There is also a Japanese silk fabric in a pale lake color, shimmering with patterns of wood grain and water ripples; at regular intervals, two plum blossoms the size of teacups float upon the water, their bold iron strokes and delicate silver lines resembling the colorful stained-glass windows of a medieval chapel, where heavy iron borders are embedded into the red glass. Most commonly found in the marketplace, however, are various unnamed colors—indistinct shades that are not quite green, not quite gray, not quite yellow, suitable only as backgrounds. These are neutral tones, also known as protective colors, civilized hues, or mixed shades."}
{"trans": "This charm comes entirely from her movements; each step she takes, each stretch of her waist, each hand brushing her hair, each glance, each lowering of her head, even the slight flutter of her sleeves, the delicate swaying of her skirt—all are as smooth as flowing honey, as gentle as a soft breeze. How could we not rejoice and praise her? Most enchanting is that soft waist of hers; the ancients described willow branches swaying in the wind, and in the \"Dream of the Red Chamber,\" Qingwen's water-snake waist were both used to depict the delicate and supple waist. But the waist I adore is as soft and sweet as Suzhou nougat, filling my mouth with sweetness and my teeth with tenderness. When the waist is this supple, her hands and feet naturally exude an extraordinary grace and elegance."}
{"trans": "Leaning at odd angles were several wine bottles, though there was hardly any wine left in them. Unfortunately, I don't drink; otherwise, at such a moment, a few sips would surely be a delightful pleasure—\"Raise my cup to invite the bright moon,\" and the moon would shyly slip into your glass. A gentle breeze swept by, rustling the forests on both mountainsides; as the branches swayed, the lights flickered even more evasively, like mischievous children playing hide-and-seek with you, harmonizing with the shimmering reflections dancing upon the river’s surface, as if performing together in a symphony. What an earthly dream this must be!"}
{"trans": "I can no longer clearly explain why there should be such a sense of melancholy on the stage, illuminated by real sunlight. There is a place where art and reality overlap, becoming hazy and indistinct; it's as if holding a match alight in the sunlight, flickering vaguely, the pale orange-yellow flame barely visible, yet one can feel more distinctly one's own hand as something temporary within the sunlight itself... On the stage, the maid sang for a while, then, balancing a tea tray in her hands, she gracefully passed through rooms and courtyards, crossing countless thresholds until she reached the study, where she bowed deeply to the young master and raised the tea tray to her eyebrows."}
{"trans": "I saw a tortoiseshell cat lounging sideways beneath a crumbling, abandoned section of wall, morning glories bursting forth in a kaleidoscope of deep green and vibrant purple, while the cat indifferently stretched its limbs. In the hazy darkness, I noticed how the streetlight projected the shadow of the transformer box onto a blank construction-site wall, interwoven with the swaying silhouettes of roadside trees, blending reality and illusion—looking just like the balcony where Romeo sang his serenade to Juliet. I saw Poet Zhou Mengdie's face perfectly framed within a small window of a departing bus as I waved him off, as though the entire vehicle, in a most solemn manner, had become a grand picture frame for him."}
{"trans": "Imagine that innocent heart, unencumbered yet loving everything, clearly seen within the vague morning mist; no matter how eagerly you beckon with your hands, it simply will not return to your chest—how incomplete this is! Thus, Mr. Pingbo feels restless and, in an honest and straightforward way, like a gentle spring breeze whispering among green trees, softly and intimately recounts to you his cherished yet elusive \"childhood.\" Although he cannot remain forever in that \"childhood,\" if he could only invite a few companions to wander through its memories together, he might slightly ease his feeling of emptiness, and that melancholy taste would not constantly linger on his tongue."}
{"trans": "You could also say it is the starting point for the Chinese people's journey towards modernity, but which nation, in its march toward modernity, has ever moved with steps as hurried, frantic, self-doubting, and disordered as those in Shanghai? You could further argue that it is an urban civilization rising in opposition to agrarian civilization, yet what other urban civilization remains as constantly threatened by the covetousness, disintegration, encirclement, and overshadowing of an immense rural force as Shanghai does? In short, it is a grand paradox: when you gaze upon its filth, it bursts forth dazzling brilliance; when you revere its power, it turns around to show you the scarred and battered wall behind it."}
{"trans": "However, the truth is quite the opposite. Sitting there quietly, I listened to the pattering of the raindrops above. At that moment, sound surpassed silence, and I felt boundless joy in my heart, as if I had sipped celestial dew and imbibed sacred nectar, nearly feeling as though I were soaring into the heavens. The sound varied—sometimes slow, sometimes fast; sometimes high, sometimes low; sometimes loud, sometimes soft; sometimes continuous, sometimes intermittent. At times it was like golden chimes and jade vibrations; at times like the grand resonance of mighty bells; at times like large and small pearls falling upon a jade plate; at times like red coral and white amber sinking into the sea; at times like the playing of a simple zither; at times like the dance of lightning; at times like the competing songs of hundreds of birds; at times like the fall of a hare and the swoop of a falcon. My thoughts soared beyond control, my heart blossomed with delight, and words flowed effortlessly from my brush."}
{"trans": "The surroundings were cluttered with numerous billboards and shops, car horns honking incessantly; he was that man from the ancient legendary tale who experienced the Huang Liang dream. Yet he had merely taken a brief nap and awakened without having such a dream himself—there was instead a certain sense of pity. The Taoist priest approached a hardware store, prostrated himself before its entrance, and naturally, no one gave him money. He seemed indifferent, bowing once into the dust before rising again. \"Tuo—tuo—\" he tapped his staff and moved to the front of the neighboring tobacco and sundries shop, again \"kneeling low in the dirt,\" his head hanging sideways. His movement was like a dark sluggish stream, resembling a black chrysanthemum slowly blooming open."}
{"trans": "What of it? Birds sing in spring, insects chirp in autumn, mosquitoes hum like thunder in summer. At night, insects stir while birds sleep. Wind and rain do not occur every day; dogs do not bark without cause, and hens do not crow unless they have laid eggs. Only humans constantly produce sounds, using speech, gestures, and machines at any time and place. Even when alone in a room, with no one to talk to, a person can turn on a record player, listen to the radio, or even snore loudly during sleep. Language certainly is not merely sound; yet when words are unpleasant, unwelcome, or overheard from behind walls or from a distance, they lose their sharpness and clarity, becoming a fluctuating din, as meaningless as the crowing of a rooster or the barking of a dog."}
{"trans": "With the passage of time, the past remains forever gone, unable to rewind to that first encounter beneath the blooming peach trees; yet within human memory, those lingering emotions or lingering sorrows often return like waves that lap against the shore, making the present moment an extension of these past feelings, stretching onward further and ever further still.\n\nIf life were a blank book already bound and numbered, the disturbances left by past emotions would resemble ink pressed too forcefully through the pages, leaving indelible stains that cannot be erased.\n\nCertainly, there is no need to destroy those old pages merely for satisfaction, just as, once the yellow crane has flown away, there would be no reason to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower; however, under lamplight, when we unfold these old records, knowing when to proceed and when to stop is indeed necessary."}
{"trans": "The Northwest is a land of barren basalt mountains and vast deserts where lone smoke rises straight toward the sky. As a geologist, you carry a large canvas geological bag slung over your shoulder, and you've been on the move for twenty years. Twenty years of tents, adrift like a small boat upon seas of shifting sand dunes, under the cold glow of a crescent moon. Can the bell chimes of Hanshan Temple beyond Suzhou's city walls still reach a traveler's boat at midnight? Your wife, that beautiful maiden as delicate as jade and blossoms, gazes longingly toward you. The web of yearning spreads across her face as she tries to fish back a loving heart that has drifted away. You return once every year, each time planting a grove of bamboo by your doorstep before leaving again. All you leave behind are clusters of bamboo leaves forming the shape of the character \"ge\" (个)."}
{"trans": "If life is a blank book already bound and paginated, then the disturbance caused by past emotions is akin to pressing too hard with the pen while writing on a page, allowing the ink to bleed through to the following pages, leaving an indelible mark. Of course, one need not destroy the old pages merely to achieve peace of mind, just as once the yellow crane has flown away, why should one destroy the Yellow Crane Tower? However, it is essential to unfold the old records by lamplight, proceeding where one should proceed, and stopping where one should stop. After fully embracing life, one can view both past and new events with tolerance and generosity, giving them their rightful place and meaning. If an event is beautiful, one can discern from its bud what kind of branch has sprouted; if it is sorrowful, one can also see a tender shoot stretching from cloudy skies into the sunshine."}
{"trans": "Everything felt distant from me, even my own shadow under the bright moonlight seemed blurrier than smoke. Just as I thought of turning to sleep; somehow my steps hesitated for a moment, causing the fleeting dream, like an arrow in flight, to suddenly pause, though it immediately resumed racing away like an arrow shedding its tip."}
{"trans": "The final hope is purely an aesthetic support. Like a shipwreck in icy seas beyond any salvation, raising one's head for a final glance at the surging dark clouds; like facing certain death beneath a hail of swords, lowering one's head to witness the splatter of blood. Aesthetic support is the ultimate support."}
{"trans": "What we gather from past and future are but grains of seed. When you are a wish wandering in the mist, I too wander there the same. We seek each other; from our longing, dreams arise—those dreams endless, those dreams boundless and vast."}
{"trans": "In such purity, the dish is oneself, the cook is oneself, and the eater is still oneself. Just as love is oneself, the one who knows this love is oneself, and the one who recalls this love is still oneself. One savors oneself bite by bite, across the cup of time, and thus intoxicates oneself."}
{"trans": "Long pants cling tightly, my steps paralyzed. My heart is as pure as a blank sheet of paper, as empty as a newborn babe. I bid farewell to the sea, to a lonely seagull circling in the sky—I will return to speak of the dust from the eight corners of the earth and the nine realms of heaven. I pick up the umbrella and shoes, gathering the myriad things of the mortal world."}
{"trans": "Unpredictable. I only hope that even as a human flaw, it should properly assume a dignified form. Like a noble warrior's furrowed brow and sigh, rather than a group of ragged soldiers brawling in the dead of night; like two snow-capped peaks standing in solemn opposition for a thousand years, rather than a tangle of wild vines clinging to a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night, the plateau was breathtakingly beautiful. The sky resembled a deep blue ritual object crafted during the Jingtai era of the Ming Dynasty, its expanse infinitely deep and boundless. Even through the moon's vast silver disk, the metallic blue glow behind it remained visible. The moonlight could not withstand the sky's cerulean stain, dissipating like diluted ink in delicate, wispy threads."}
{"trans": "Watching the same movie repeatedly is like vomiting up food and chewing it again. At that moment, our heads turned golden, as if covered with a layer of wheat spikes. I recall a character in Gorky's book once said that lovers from youth should not meet again, like a skeleton rising from the ground..."}
{"trans": "When I close my eyes, I think of it; when I open them, I crave it. But when all of this rushes toward me, nearly drowning me, I can hardly tell what I truly want anymore. I feel only a heartache, as if my heart is being tightly bound by silken threads, scorched drop by drop by candle tears, and tossed about on the vast, surging sea."}
{"trans": "The faintest echo of your sobs will become it; after life is veiled, it, like your greatest soul, is covered and hidden. When life speaks, all the winds become words; when life speaks again, the smile on your lips and the tears in your eyes will also become words."}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality has increasingly faded. With the passing of seasons, plum blossoms wither and cranes age; culture has become a purposeless waste, and the closed-loop pursuit of moral perfection has led to overall immorality. Civilizational advancement has thus been halted, leaving behind only a pile of plum petals and crane feathers, like bookmarks inserted into the annals of the nation's spiritual history."}
{"trans": "Approving religious spirit based on science and philosophy is akin to approaching a romantic relationship with intellect and reasoning, which suppresses the passion of life and drains the allure of love. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is like treating family status and wealth as conditions for marriage, turning children into breeding machines and producing spiritual eunuchs."}
{"trans": "In fact, all acts of destruction are tangible, all grievances are difficult to articulate, and therefore those answers are also suspect. What should not be doubted is the outcome: withered grass and rubble bear the weight of one disaster after another, from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face all of this in a perilous situation devoid of any protective mechanisms, just as one would remove gloves to gently touch an elderly person's scars."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written so many pages. I see myself as a child, copying down a verse from a long hymn; the angels sang that hymn when God shaped the first human. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person, memorizing a sentence from a book written by Wisdom; that book was inscribed on the heart's first page before time began."}
{"trans": "Even if it is an event spanning millennia, even if it is an achievement connecting thousands of miles, if it belongs to culture, it is often borne by a single pair of aged shoulders. Like smugglers, like fugitives, dodging all the way, conducting undercover investigations all the way, seeking a place for entrustment. The decision of entrustment is always written in a will, thus inevitably destined to be unable to elucidate the cultural significance of one's life while still alive."}
{"trans": "Undoubtedly, the result is one of desolation—withered grass and broken tiles, bearing the traces of countless disasters from ancient times to the present. I am willing to face all of this in a perilous situation devoid of any protective mechanisms, just as one would remove their gloves to touch the scars of an elderly person. This act of touching often leads to deep contemplation: as the foundation of our existence, Chinese civilization is also riddled with scars, yet how has it managed to avoid a systemic collapse?"}
{"trans": "Is there anyone who can attach pre-made meaning to your birth certificate and give it to you? Being born is in itself a demand for meaning, asking you to search for or create meaning, much like a publishing contract with an advance fee already paid, with a deadline lasting a lifetime. Of course, you are not the creditor but the debtor; it is life that demands meaning from you, leaving you no room to complain."}
{"trans": "Those uneven ink smudges, those red-printed headlines, those names crossed out with Xs, those rows of exclamation marks, those stiff appeals, those repeated corrections—combined into a chilling sound that rushed straight at us. Just like how a few strands of white hair caught on a spiderweb in a corner, or half a piece of torn cloth tangled among withered leaves at the treetops, could instantly transport us back to that era we dare not recall."}
{"trans": "Some fall upon the hair bun of the vegetable-gathering woman, some stick to the swallows' black coats, some slip into the small river to frolic in the water. The river, like a thousand wandering flute players, accompanies the children leaving school in their singing and revelry. When mischievous children balance their books atop yellow leather hats, holding two shoes in hand and wading through the river, might a spore-baby pop out from the flute's hole, bite the hem of the child's garment, and finally return to the wild fern mother's soil?"}
{"trans": "Soul, return! Come back to your ancestral home! When he spoke the Minnan dialect and caused people to burst into laughter, when he spoke the Beijing dialect and left them exchanging puzzled glances, why did he never defend himself? Here, his Chu dialect is as profound as the mountains and rivers, as grand as the heavens and spirits. Every note from the master of ceremonies sounds like the voice of a father reading the \"Chen Qing Biao\"—melancholic and sorrowful, each note wounds you deeply."}
{"trans": "He was too thin; his dry skin could not fill the gaps between his ribs, so that his flat abdomen resembled a steel bridge spanning across the bony arches. His intense, heavy heartbeat was like a bleeding sun, burning hollowly and echoing with the sounds of flames and caverns. Mei Ying had heard Yue Beizhi's heartbeat—deep and resonant, passing through his well-developed muscles, the heart like coal buried deep within the earth's crust, pulsing steadily and rhythmically."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, never having settled in a mountain village or by the water's edge, what talisman can I pray for? Perhaps youth—but how fleeting it is. I am like someone who has unearthed treasure, carrying pearls and gold in a leaky mesh bag, only to discover along the way that the burden grows ever lighter—youth has scattered into dust. Perhaps the scriptures and classical texts—but can a belly full of knowledge mend the broken mirror in my hand?"}
{"trans": "On the mountain ridges of my hometown, greetings are exchanged from afar, never in the soft and limp \"Hey—\" of city dwellers, nor in the exaggerated, feigned surprise of southerners, \"Wow—\"—for such sounds cannot travel far before the mountains swallow them whole. Only the deep, heavy, lingering, and desolate \"Eh-ha—\" can soar like a bald eagle, lingering long in flight. Today, this eagle's cry falls like mist from the sky, and boundless homesickness burns fiercely within Shen Zhanping's chest."}
{"trans": "Hurry up and escape from the political quagmire that you yourself do not even remotely understand, and go chase after the long-lost poetic sentiment. Chasing poetic sentiment is equally chasing oneself—the self once known throughout China, the self once clung to by one's wife, the self that seemed to have been found yet was actually lost. This time, turning back to chase after it, one is accompanied by morning glow, witnessed by river currents, encouraged by the cries of apes, and cleared a path by ten thousand mountains. Thus, the vessel of life, which had become increasingly burdened and heavy, once again becomes a light vessel."}
{"trans": "An airplane, though it may be likened to Zhuangzi's carefree journey or Liezi's ride upon the wind, lacks visual staying power. How could it compare to the long journeys of trains, with their hypnotic rhythm and ever-changing scenery, offering a view as if through a window—both immersed in the world yet seemingly removed from it? Therefore, during my travels overseas, whenever the clattering double tracks reach a destination, I always stand on the platform—aptly named the \"long pavilion\"—waiting for the rugged masculinity of the train as it roars and surges forward relentlessly, coming to carry me toward distant horizons."}
{"trans": "In contrast to prominence lies normalcy; in contrast to officialdom lies the common people. To vanish into the ordinary life of a small town offers more effective concealment than grass and trees in the mountains. Concealment in the mountains still retains and displays a kind of aloofness, and aloof concealment is ultimately insincere. Concealment within the streets of a small town not only avoids deliberate torment and destruction of life, but even allows one to live comfortably, enabling life to fit quietly into a convenient niche, almost dissolving oneself entirely from inside out. Thus, this becomes the highest form of concealment. Perhaps calling it concealment is too narrow. In my eyes, scenes like small bridges over flowing rivers and homes amidst tranquil landscapes, along with nostalgic longings, all represent ecological images of a deeply spiritual philosophy of life."}
{"trans": "The spring breeze knows me not; why does it enter my gauze curtains?"}
{"trans": "Henceforth, I have no heart to love the fair night;  \nLet the bright moon set on the western pavilion."}
{"trans": "The candle, with a heart, still mourns the farewell,  \nShedding tears on our behalf until dawn."}
{"trans": "Chang'e must regret stealing the elixir,  \nEmerald sea and azure sky, night after night."}
{"trans": "The Three Visits brought forth the grand strategy for the empire; Through two dynasties, the old minister's heart opened and sustained the realm."}
{"trans": "The tripartite division entwines strategies, Through endless ages, a single feather soars in the heavens."}
{"trans": "\"A gardenia's song, unbearable in its sorrow.\""}
{"trans": "The swallows that once graced the halls of the noble Wang and Xie now fly into the homes of common folk."}
{"trans": "Melancholy without reason to meet Fan Li; Uneven misty trees east of the Five Lakes."}
{"trans": "If the east wind had not aided Zhou Yu, the two Qiaos would have been locked in the Bronze Bird Tower deep in spring."}
{"trans": "Victory and defeat, the unforeseen affairs of generals; To bear shame and endure humiliation, that is a true man."}
{"trans": "How could forty-eight years as emperor not equal the Lu family's Mo Chou?"}
{"trans": "Jade token departs the phoenix palace gate; iron cavalry encircles the dragon city."}
{"trans": "Why should the Qiang flute lament the willow? The spring breeze does not cross the Jade Gate Pass."}
{"trans": "Amidst the yellow sands, a hundred battles don golden armor;  \nWe shall not return until Loulan is broken."}
{"trans": "The moon of the Qin dynasty, the passes of the Han,  \nTen thousand li of campaign, the men have not returned."}
{"trans": "The frontier guard gazes at the border's hue,  \nYearning for home, his face etched with sorrow."}
{"trans": "To shoot a rider, first shoot his horse; to capture bandits, first capture their king."}
{"trans": "The boundless sea is lined with ice cliffs a hundred zhang high; sorrowful clouds stretch bleakly across ten thousand miles of frozen expanse."}
{"trans": "Dark woods, the wind alarms the grass;  \nThe general draws his bow by night."}
{"trans": "The sands of the vast desert lie like snow,  \nThe moon above Yanshan curves like a hook."}
{"trans": "Under the midday sun I weed the crops,\nMy sweat drips onto the soil below."}
{"trans": "A rider dashes through the red dust, the imperial concubine smiles;  \nNo one knows it's the lychees that have arrived."}
{"trans": "A dappled horse, a fur coat worth a thousand gold,  \nCall the boy, bring them forth to trade for wine,  \nTogether with you, I'll drown all timeless sorrows."}
{"trans": "Wanting to cross the Yellow River, ice blocks the stream; About to climb the Taihang Mountains, snow fills the peaks."}
{"trans": "The Emperor summoned him, but he refused to board the ship; He claimed himself to be the wine immortal."}
{"trans": "Nature concentrates divine beauty; Yin and Yang cleave dusk from dawn."}
{"trans": "I have a lost soul that cannot be summoned,  \nAt the rooster's single cry, the world turns white."}
{"trans": "I muse on the vast eternity of heaven and earth;  \nAlone, I feel a sudden sorrow and tears fall."}
{"trans": "Boundless trees shed leaves in rustling descent; endless Yangtze surges onward."}
{"trans": "Gay with the spring wind, my horse's hooves fly fast,  \nIn one day, I view all the flowers of Chang'an."}
{"trans": "Zhuangzi's morning dream captivated by butterflies, Wang Di entrusts his spring heart to the cuckoo."}
{"trans": "The solitary smoke rises straight in the vast desert; The setting sun is round over the long river."}
{"trans": "Sitting alone in the quiet bamboo grove, playing the zither and then humming a tune."}
{"trans": "A cascade of three thousand feet falls straight down, As if the Milky Way had fallen from the ninth heaven."}
{"trans": "The window frames the timeless snow of the western ridge; the door moors the distant ships from Eastern Wu."}
{"trans": "Wild flowers in full bloom gradually dazzle the eyes; tender grass just covers the horse hooves."}
{"trans": "The Southern Dynasties had four hundred and eighty temples; how many pavilions and terraces are shrouded in mist and rain."}
{"trans": "When Qingming comes with drizzling rain,  \nTravelers on the road are overwhelmed with sorrow."}
{"trans": "Who shaped these slender leaves so fine? The February breeze, like scissors sharp."}
{"trans": "All fragrant flowers have faded by April in the world; At the mountain temple, peach blossoms are just beginning to bloom."}
{"trans": "Under heaven, a bosom friend exists; at the ends of the earth, they are as close as neighbors."}
{"trans": "Should friends and kin in Luoyang inquire, my heart's pure ice within a jade pot."}
{"trans": "I urge you to drink another cup of wine,  \nFor westward past the Yang Pass, no old friends will be found."}
{"trans": "I send my sorrowful heart to the bright moon, to accompany you all the way to the west of Yelang."}
{"trans": "Though the Peach Blossom Pool runs a thousand feet deep,  \nStill it's not as deep as Master Wang's parting gift of feeling true."}
{"trans": "A lone sail fades into the azure sky's expanse,  \nOnly the Yangtze flows to the horizon's edge."}
{"trans": "The temple in the deep bamboo grove, where the distant bell tolls at dusk."}
{"trans": "Nearer home, my heart's more timid;  \nI dare not ask the passerby."}
{"trans": "Tonight, the Willow-Breaking Song is heard in the melody; Who does not feel longing for their homeland?"}
{"trans": "War flames for three months; A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold."}
{"trans": "Who can say that the heart of an inch-long grass can repay the radiant spring sunshine?"}
{"trans": "The flute's melody drifts through the reeds,  \nWhite birds in line suddenly take flight."}
{"trans": "Tide riders stand atop the waves' crest,  \nHolding the red flag aloft, the flag stays dry."}
{"trans": "Lush and countless, the roads run north, south, east, and west."}
{"trans": "The morning chill is light beyond the misty green willows;  \nThe red apricot branches teem with spring's lively cheer."}
{"trans": "Early rest on the fragrant grass path halfway; In late spring, still chilly and about to rain."}
{"trans": "The fragrance comes late with the gentle night breeze; unbeknownst to me, by dawn, blossoms cover all the south-facing boughs."}
{"trans": "Why bother with light green or deep red hues? They are indeed the finest among flowers."}
{"trans": "If trees had feelings, they wouldn't be so green!"}
{"trans": "Cold moonlight, dewy chill; parasol leaves turn and fall, golden."}
{"trans": "Ever since our parting, on the Jing Shu Tower, the moonlight flowed like water."}
{"trans": "When night deepens, the wind stills, and it's time to return,  \nOnly a river of bright moonlight, green as glass, remains."}
{"trans": "Dream severed from the homeland's mountains and rivers, separated by layers of misty waters."}
{"trans": "The knot of unity on the silken girdle remains unformed;  \nThe tide at the river's head has already calmed."}
{"trans": "Thinking of departure, a thousand miles of misty waves,  \nThe heavy evening haze stretches across the vast Chu sky."}
{"trans": "With tearful eyes I ask the flowers, but they do not speak; The scattered red petals fly past the swing and away."}
{"trans": "Amidst falling blossoms, a lone person stands; In the gentle rain, swallows fly in pairs."}
{"trans": "A thousand miles away lies the lonely grave; nowhere to speak of the desolation."}
{"trans": "Every day I think of you but cannot see you; we share the waters of the Yangtze River."}
{"trans": "Though the mountain vows endure, a brocade letter is hard to deliver."}
{"trans": "The old affairs of the Six Dynasties have passed with the flowing river; only cold mists and withered grasses remain, their green now deepened."}
{"trans": "With a feather fan and silk scarf, amidst laughter and talk, the enemy's ships are reduced to smoke and ashes."}
{"trans": "At night, the sound of a honking crane was heard; all proclaimed the arrival of the royal army."}
{"trans": "A son should be like Sun Zhongmou!"}
{"trans": "Thirty years of merit and fame are dust and earth;  \nEight thousand miles of road through clouds and moon."}
{"trans": "At the Fuli Shrine, a sight of sacred crows and the drums of the village festival."}
{"trans": "Returning home inebriated, caressing the sword while leaning into the west wind,  \nThe river's surging waves still fortify one's resolve."}
{"trans": "The river surges like a whale's charge, the mountains crouch like tigers in their form; the natural barrier is not man-made."}
{"trans": "Towers lost in mist, moonlight confuses ferry crossings."}
{"trans": "The Qiang flute plays in clear weather, lotus songs drift through the night; joyful old fishermen and lotus girls."}
{"trans": "In the fragrance of rice blossoms, we speak of a bountiful year. Listen to the chorus of frogs."}
{"trans": "A hundred fleeting years of rise and fall have passed, yet you and I still behold the same moon as then."}
{"trans": "Helplessly, the flowers fall away; The swallows return, as if we've met before."}
{"trans": "At the foot of the mountain, orchid sprouts barely reach the stream,  \nThrough the pines, the sandy path lies clean and free of mud,  \nIn the drizzling evening rain, the cuckoo's cry resounds."}
{"trans": "The Chinese parasol trees are mingled with a drizzle,  \nBy dusk, the drops fall one by one."}
{"trans": "Swallows fly in, inquiring where spring resides; only the pond remains green of itself."}
{"trans": "I wish to ride the wind and return home, yet I fear the jade pavilions and crystal palaces, for the heights are too cold to bear."}
{"trans": "Clearly, a sudden awakening from the Huaxu dream,  \nLooking back, the east wind fills my robe with tears."}
{"trans": "The Chu sky stretches a thousand miles in clear autumn; waters flow with the sky into boundless autumn."}
{"trans": "Red beans grow in the southern land. When spring comes, how many branches sprout?"}
{"trans": "The sun rises in the east while rain falls in the west. Though they say there's no fair weather, there is."}
{"trans": "At the Xie Pavilion where farewells occur, the scenery ever brings sorrow."}
{"trans": "His merits surpassed the Three Kingdoms,  \nHis fame was realized through the Eight Formations."}
{"trans": "When the flowers bloom, pick them straight away; don't wait until there are no flowers left to break the branches in vain."}
{"trans": "The sunset is infinitely beautiful, yet it heralds the dusk."}
{"trans": "Lovely is the third night of early September,  \nDewdrops gleam like pearls, the moon a silver bow."}
{"trans": "After gathering nectar from myriad flowers to make honey,  \nFor whom is the toil, for whom is the sweetness?"}
